' =====================================================================
'  Annotated class diagram — self-contained (single file, no !include).
'
'  Scope: the export/ package — concrete Exporter implementations.
'  The Exporter seam itself moved into core/engine/ (see
'  Class_Diagram/class_diag_commented.puml) once WorldEngine grew its
'  own optional `exporter` field — WorldEngine.advance_time_step()
'  calls exporter.record() directly, no wrapper class needed. export/
'  supplies the concrete side only, the same shape as pibt/ supplying
'  a concrete PathPlanner: depends on core/, core/ does not know it
'  exists. core/ classes referenced here (WorldEngine, Exporter, Agent,
'  AssignmentManifest) are shown as stubs; see
'  Class_Diagram/class_diag_commented.puml for their real detail.
'
'  Regenerate with:
'      plantuml diagrammes/Class_Diagram/Export/class_diag_commented.puml
'
'  Output:
'      export_class_diagram_commente.png
' =====================================================================

@startuml export_class_diagram_commente
title Simulation — export/ class diagram (annotated: context & design patterns)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ClassBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassHeaderFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #888888
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam linetype ortho

' =====================================================================
'  core — stubs only; this package's real home is Class_Diagram/
' =====================================================================
package "core (stubs)" #EAF4FF {
    class WorldEngine
    abstract class Exporter
    class Agent
    class AssignmentManifest
}

' =====================================================================
'  export — concrete Exporters; no seam of its own, core owns that now
' =====================================================================
package "export" #FFF3E0 {

    class TraceCsvExporter {
        - _csv_path : Path
        - _rows     : list[tuple]
        --
        + rows() : list[tuple]
        + record(step, agents, grid, outcome, intent) : void
        + flush() : void
    }
    note bottom of TraceCsvExporter
      **Per-tick trace, and AggregateCsvExporter's data source**
      One row per agent per tick: step, agent_id, x, y, orientation,
      read off `agents` alone. rows() exposes them read-only so
      AggregateCsvExporter reuses this instead of re-reading agents.
      Ignores grid, outcome and intent.
    end note

    class AggregateCsvExporter {
        - _csv_path : Path
        - _trace    : TraceCsvExporter
        - _goals    : dict[tuple, Coordinates2D]
        --
        + record(step, agents, grid, outcome, intent) : void
        + flush() : void
    }
    note bottom of AggregateCsvExporter
      **Per-run summary, appended**
      record() only reads intent.goals, keyed by (step, agent_id) —
      not fixed at construction, so a rotating goal (lifelong) still
      counts a fresh arrival per assignment. flush() pairs that with
      _trace.rows() for position, then appends one row (date,
      n_agents, ticks, success_rate, makespan, deadlocks) to a
      shared CSV instead of overwriting it.
    end note

    class CompositeExporter {
        - _exporters : list[Exporter]
        --
        + record(step, agents, grid, outcome, intent) : void
        + flush() : void
    }
    note bottom of CompositeExporter
      **Fan-out, not a new seam**
      Wraps several Exporters behind one — WorldEngine.exporter
      still holds exactly one object. Forwards record()/flush() to
      each, so one run can feed both TraceCsvExporter and
      AggregateCsvExporter.
    end note
}

TraceCsvExporter --|> Exporter
AggregateCsvExporter --|> Exporter
CompositeExporter --|> Exporter

TraceCsvExporter ..> Agent : «reads»

AggregateCsvExporter ..> AssignmentManifest : «reads»

' Hollow: AggregateCsvExporter is handed a TraceCsvExporter the caller
' also owns (and may attach separately, e.g. inside the same
' CompositeExporter) — a shared reference, not an exclusive one, same
' reasoning as CompositeExporter -> Exporter just below. Both exporters
' still see every tick independently via record(); the coupling only
' matters at flush() time, once _trace.rows() is complete.
AggregateCsvExporter "1" o-- "1" TraceCsvExporter : _trace

' Hollow: CompositeExporter is handed already-constructed exporters and
' holds references to them — the same "shared, not owned" shape as
' WorldEngine o-- Exporter in the main diagram, not an exclusive-owner
' composition.
CompositeExporter "1" o-- "1..*" Exporter : _exporters

' =====================================================================
'  Page-level legend — the 30-second read.
' =====================================================================
legend bottom left
  **What this diagram covers**
  export/: concrete Exporters plugged into WorldEngine.exporter.
  TraceCsvExporter logs the raw per-tick trace; AggregateCsvExporter
  reuses it (_trace) instead of re-reading agents, so position data
  is read once, not duplicated. CompositeExporter fans record()/
  flush() out to both. Depends only on core/, the same one-directional
  shape as pibt/.
end legend

@enduml
